 "notes": "Headline 95% CL upper limit on the dark-photon kinetic mixing epsilon (=chi) from patchy dark screening of the CMB (Planck NPIPE x unWISE Blue+Green cross-correlation). Traced the red 'Joint' curve in Fig.3 (constraints_newrange_ellmin2_withbias_nodrop.png, a raster PNG; no ancillary data). The plotted variable is epsilon itself, reported directly as chi (no chi^2). Curve is the lower boundary of the red excluded region: exclusion is epsilon > curve. Axis calibration from tick marks: x col165=1e-13 eV (188 px/decade), y row26=1e-5 (112.67 px/decade). Minimum epsilon ~3.6e-8 near m_A' ~4e-13 eV; consistent with the paper's stated eps<4e-8 over the range 1e-13 - 1e-11 eV and best sensitivity at m_A'~5e-13 eV. This is not a dark-matter-density-dependent search (resonant CMB photon->DP conversion), so dm_density_assumed is null. Scan range 1.5e-13 to 9.7e-12 eV; steep left/right walls at ~1.7e-13 and ~5e-12 eV bound the excluded region.",
